{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Grammar and examples consistency",
  "description": "Keeps docs/grammar.md, the bundled examples in src/examples, and the compile prompt in agreement whenever any of them changes.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "docs/grammar.md",
      "src/examples/**/*.ts",
      "src/compile/prompt.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "docs/grammar.md, src/examples/ or src/compile/prompt.ts changed. These three must agree: the EBNF and prose in docs/grammar.md define the language, src/examples/index.ts holds the six example scripts byte-for-byte as they appear under '## 8. Example scripts' in docs/grammar.md (same ids, same descriptions, same scripts), and src/compile/prompt.ts embeds docs/grammar.md plus those examples. Do the following: 1) Run `npm test -- src/examples src/compile` which includes the consistency test and the prompt snapshot. 2) If docs/grammar.md changed, diff the EBNF against src/parser (keywords in the lexer table, statement forms in the parser) and report any construct that is in one but not the other. 3) If an example script or description changed in either place, copy the change to the other place so they are byte-identical, then confirm every example still parses by running the tests again. 4) If the prompt snapshot changed, update it only if the grammar or examples changed on purpose; otherwise explain the drift. Reply with a short list of what was in sync, what you changed, and anything you could not reconcile. Never edit the acceptance criteria in .kiro/specs/flip-card/requirements.md from this hook."
  }
}
